(Bug #45 — the right column. A call whose return type was never declared is
 refused only where nothing supplies a type. A declared variable supplies
 one, at the declaration and at every later reassignment, so this is the way
 out the diagnostic names and it must keep working exactly as it did.)

To 'opaque label'. Return "hi".

a text called saved is 'opaque label'.
print saved.
print "got {saved}".

a text called later is "placeholder".
the later is 'opaque label'.
print later.

a list called items is [].
append saved to items.
print element 1 of items.
